WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:03.294
[Rafiq] رَفِيق. In Arabic, it means companion.

2
00:00:03.794 --> 00:00:08.528
That's what this app was made to be: a companion for anyone studying Arabic.

3
00:00:09.228 --> 00:00:15.563
In a class, at a madrasa, or on your own, lessons give you new words. Keeping them is the hard part.

4
00:00:16.163 --> 00:00:19.832
So we built رَفِيق around three findings from memory research.

5
00:00:20.532 --> 00:00:28.068
Spacing. Coming back to a word after a gap beats cramming. It's one of the most replicated findings in memory research.

6
00:00:28.767 --> 00:00:33.164
Testing. Pulling a word from memory strengthens it more than reading it again.

7
00:00:33.864 --> 00:00:37.440
Habit. A few minutes every day beats an hour once a week.

8
00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:41.273
[Rafiq] رَفِيق gives you a small daily goal, and a streak to keep.

9
00:00:41.974 --> 00:00:48.996
[Rafiq] So رَفِيق brings each word back after a day, then two, four, eight, and asks you to recall it, not just reread it.

10
00:00:49.796 --> 00:00:54.094
Use it to revise alongside your course. Or start from nothing at all.

11
00:00:54.793 --> 00:00:59.886
Can't read Arabic yet? Begin with the twenty-eight letters, in families that share a shape.

12
00:01:00.586 --> 00:01:05.465
Every letter comes with three words, the letter in red, and a native voice to copy.

13
00:01:05.815 --> 00:01:06.794
بَيْت — house

14
00:01:07.594 --> 00:01:11.185
Then the vowel marks, and a listening test to train your ear.

15
00:01:11.585 --> 00:01:12.564
سَمَك — fish

16
00:01:14.764 --> 00:01:17.708
From your first letter to your first conversation.

17
00:01:18.908 --> 00:01:21.534
A few minutes a day, with a companion beside you.

18
00:01:22.034 --> 00:01:25.935
[Rafiq] Start your first lesson free at rafiq-arabic.com.
